1
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:11,570
Prosecutor,

2
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:13,890
Cheng Jia definitely did this.

3
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:15,240
I swear on my life.

4
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:19,160
Besides, I've been
Ms. Cui's secretary for years.

5
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:20,820
She recognized my potential.

6
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:22,720
Now she's gone so mysteriously.

7
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:24,900
I have to seek justice for her.

8
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:26,600
You said in your previous testimony

9
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:28,000
that Cheng Jia premeditated this.

10
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:29,000
What did you mean?

11
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:30,360
You're absolutely right.

12
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:31,820
She had it all planned out.

13
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:35,160
She was still holding a grudge
over that incident.

14
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:36,820
She just couldn't get over it.

15
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:43,840
Actually,

16
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:45,370
I've been thinking lately.

17
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:47,360
I really didn't think things through

18
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:49,240
regarding that matter,

19
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:51,600
and completely ignored your feelings.

20
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:54,220
I sincerely apologize to you.

21
00:00:58,200 --> 00:00:59,130
Are you serious?

22
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:01,880
Of course I am.

23
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:05,200
We built this company together.

24
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:07,700
We can't let this cause a rift between us.

25
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:11,560
Actually,

26
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:13,440
I was partly at fault
for what happened last time.

27
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:15,240
I shouldn't have yelled at you.

28
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:20,760
It's all my fault.

29
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:22,320
I

30
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:24,800
shouldn't have lost my temper with you.

31
00:01:25,080 --> 00:01:26,320
Ultimately,

32
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:28,560
neither of us was wrong.

33
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:30,490
We just lacked communication.

34
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:31,920
Let's just

35
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,180
put this behind us.

36
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:37,120
But

37
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:40,340
about that professional manager...

38
00:01:40,479 --> 00:01:41,560
He's gone.

39
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:42,820
I fired him a while ago.

40
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:44,940
It's just the two of us from now on.

41
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:46,720
I'll do whatever you say.

42
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:49,250
I really didn't know
what to think at the time.

43
00:01:49,759 --> 00:01:51,360
I was actually quite touched

44
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:53,210
that she came to apologize.

45
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:55,680
So I had even less reason to kill her.

46
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:56,479
On the day of the incident,

47
00:01:56,479 --> 00:01:57,479
witnesses and CCTV

48
00:01:57,479 --> 00:01:59,560
confirmed you got water for Cui Xiangqin.

49
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:00,840
And we found the paper

50
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:03,120
wrapping the aspirin powder in the trash.

51
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:05,000
It was torn from your document

52
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:06,560
and has your fingerprints on it.

53
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:07,890
How do you explain that?

54
00:02:08,039 --> 00:02:09,520
I wiped the cup

55
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:13,920
after getting the water.

56
00:02:15,120 --> 00:02:17,640
Isn't that just footage of me
throwing away the tissue?

57
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:19,720
I threw away a tissue,

58
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:21,050
not that piece of paper.

59
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:22,410
Are you sure?

60
00:02:23,079 --> 00:02:24,480
I'm absolutely certain.

61
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:26,720
Do you remember

62
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:28,050
how many pills were left

63
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:30,160
the last time you used this medicine?

64
00:02:30,160 --> 00:02:31,640
About...

65
00:02:32,079 --> 00:02:33,760
ten or twenty pills,

66
00:02:33,760 --> 00:02:34,880
I guess.

67
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:35,360
But

68
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:35,820
I didn't

69
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:37,320
count them carefully.

70
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:39,920
There are only five pills
left in the bottle now.

71
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:41,360
That's quite a difference

72
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:42,040
from the ten or twenty

73
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:42,900
you mentioned.

74
00:02:44,320 --> 00:02:45,520
You have to investigate this

75
00:02:45,520 --> 00:02:47,680
thoroughly for me.

76
00:02:48,079 --> 00:02:48,920
Someone must have

77
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:50,320
stolen my pills

78
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:51,760
to frame me.

79
00:02:52,040 --> 00:02:53,240
Then why did you offer

80
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:55,579
to fetch water for Cui Xiangqin that day?

81
00:02:57,440 --> 00:02:58,100
Bingzhong,

82
00:02:58,440 --> 00:03:00,100
go check if my speech is ready.

83
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:00,770
Okay.

84
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,290
I'm out of water.

85
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:08,000
I'll get some for you.

86
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:08,330
Okay.

87
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:08,960
Thanks.

88
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:09,620
No problem.

89
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:10,850
At that time,

90
00:03:11,040 --> 00:03:12,840
Cui Bingzhong wasn't by her side.

91
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:14,560
And Cui Xiangqin needed
to take her medicine,

92
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:16,079
so I just helped her get some water.

93
00:03:16,079 --> 00:03:17,810
Isn't that perfectly logical?

94
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:18,720
It's obvious.

95
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:19,880
Cheng Jia went to get water

96
00:03:19,880 --> 00:03:21,480
just to poison the cup.

97
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:24,200
And she's been friends
with Chairman Cui for years,

98
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:25,280
so he won't mind.

99
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:26,840
Has your Chairman Cui

100
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:28,560
decided to hire a professional manager

101
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:29,760
to replace Cheng Jia?

102
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,120
They've already picked someone.

103
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:32,380
But not to replace her,

104
00:03:32,440 --> 00:03:33,920
just to help with her work.

105
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:34,930
Alright,

106
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:36,180
we understand.

107
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:38,120
Thank you for your cooperation today.

108
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:39,640
If there are any further questions,

109
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:40,770
we will contact you.

110
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:41,800
Prosecutors,

111
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:44,860
you must give Cheng Jia a harsh sentence.

112
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:52,410
You're back.

113
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:53,840
That was

114
00:03:53,840 --> 00:03:54,700
Cui Bingzhong.

115
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:57,440
He's also a distant relative
of Cui Xiangqin.

116
00:03:57,440 --> 00:03:59,970
He's been with her
since she made her fortune.

117
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:01,770
The police just called.

118
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:03,360
They've contacted Cui Xiangqin's daughter,

119
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:04,020
Liang Enqi.

120
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:06,560
She's booked the earliest flight back.

121
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:07,520
Also,

122
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:08,680
Cui Bingzhong insists that

123
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:10,520
Cheng Jia killed Cui Xiangqin.

124
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:11,800
How did it go on your end?

125
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:13,760
Pretty much the same as the case file.

126
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:15,620
Cheng Jia insists she was framed.

127
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:18,660
And Cheng Jia was very emotional,

128
00:04:18,839 --> 00:04:20,700
saying Cui Bingzhong framed her.

129
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:22,160
But Cui Bingzhong

130
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:24,320
was the first to be cleared of suspicion.

131
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:25,850
Cheng Jia was still evasive

132
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:27,040
on some questions.

133
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:28,400
Let's do a polygraph test.

134
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:28,730
Okay.

135
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,320
I'll go arrange it then.

136
00:04:30,320 --> 00:04:31,250
I'll go with you.

137
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:31,810
Let's go.

138
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:34,300
Kaixin, what's wrong?

139
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:35,159
What happened?

140
00:04:35,159 --> 00:04:36,640
Tell me, and I'll help you figure it out.

141
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:38,700
What could possibly be wrong with me?

142
00:04:38,840 --> 00:04:39,760
You say you're fine,

143
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:40,880
but I know you.

144
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:41,840
If you were really fine,

145
00:04:41,840 --> 00:04:43,000
would Prosecutor Qiao have called you out

146
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:45,400
in public during the meeting
the other day?

147
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:47,200
You wouldn't understand
even if I told you.

148
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:48,640
It's almost time to get off work, right?

149
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:50,970
I'm going to arrange the polygraph first.

150
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:52,040
If you don't want to talk now,

151
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:54,300
we can talk while playing games tonight.

152
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:58,850
Why are we eating this again today?

153
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:02,600
It's the only thing I know how to cook.

154
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:04,060
Let's just keep it simple.

155
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:06,320
What's wrong?

156
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:08,040
You've been down all day.

157
00:05:10,440 --> 00:05:11,400
Do you want to

158
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:12,520
tell me

159
00:05:12,760 --> 00:05:13,890
what's on your mind?

160
00:05:14,960 --> 00:05:15,640
Wei,

161
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:17,600
I don't think telling you

162
00:05:17,760 --> 00:05:18,640
would help.

163
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:20,920
Didn't you say

164
00:05:20,920 --> 00:05:22,360
we shouldn't hide things

165
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:23,600
and should speak up?

166
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:29,570
It's just...

167
00:05:29,920 --> 00:05:31,380
I'm really torn right now.

168
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:33,760
My mom finally agreed to let me

169
00:05:33,760 --> 00:05:35,080
work as a prosecutor,

170
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:36,440
and our relationship

171
00:05:36,440 --> 00:05:37,800
finally improved a bit.

172
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:40,440
But now she wants me to transfer
to another position.

173
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:41,370
What should I do?

174
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:45,960
I'm...

175
00:05:46,080 --> 00:05:47,640
not good at comforting people,

176
00:05:47,640 --> 00:05:49,080
but from my experience,

177
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:51,540
you should have a good talk with your mom.

178
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:56,860
Good that you know.

179
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:07,880
Hey,

180
00:06:10,520 --> 00:06:11,520
are you asleep?

181
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:13,370
I'm watching TV.

182
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:17,700
Why did you call me all of a sudden?

183
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:19,400
Miss Mom?

184
00:06:21,320 --> 00:06:22,480
Nothing much.

185
00:06:23,960 --> 00:06:24,520
Right,

186
00:06:24,520 --> 00:06:25,980
I was just about to ask you.

187
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:28,660
Did you talk to your boss
about the transfer?

188
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:31,560
I did.

189
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:32,680
I did.

190
00:06:33,280 --> 00:06:34,000
Good.

191
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:36,340
Kaixin,

192
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:38,080
Mom has been thinking

193
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:39,280
these past few days.

194
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:41,240
Why aren't you as obedient as before

195
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:42,770
since you started working?

196
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:43,600
Actually,

197
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:45,320
I don't blame you.

198
00:06:45,400 --> 00:06:46,560
The main reason is

199
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:48,290
that we communicate too little

200
00:06:48,440 --> 00:06:49,900
and have no common topics.

201
00:06:50,480 --> 00:06:52,520
Mom has been a teacher for decades.

202
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:54,800
What I'm best at

203
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:56,840
is dealing with kids.

204
00:06:57,400 --> 00:06:59,600
So after you transfer,

205
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:01,800
Mom will definitely pass on
all these decades of experience

206
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:02,760
to you.

207
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:08,880
Mom, get some rest early.

208
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:14,480
Start.

209
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:26,810
How long?

210
00:07:28,560 --> 00:07:29,290
Ten seconds.

211
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:31,000
Again.

212
00:07:34,240 --> 00:07:34,640
Start.

213
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:45,570
How about this time?

214
00:07:45,760 --> 00:07:46,690
Eleven seconds.

215
00:07:48,080 --> 00:07:48,880
One more time.

216
00:07:57,080 --> 00:07:58,010
Twelve seconds.

217
00:07:58,480 --> 00:07:59,360
The surveillance shows

218
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:01,080
the whole process took only eight seconds.

219
00:08:01,080 --> 00:08:02,080
That's not enough time

220
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:03,080
for her to drug it.

221
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:03,920
Wei,

222
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:06,100
did you open it too carefully?

223
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:08,960
She might have just torn a small opening
and poured it in.

224
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:09,690
Impossible.

225
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:11,800
I saw that paper clearly.

226
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:13,330
There was no opening at all.

227
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:16,000
Tell you what,

228
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:17,680
let's not pour the medicine this time.

229
00:08:17,680 --> 00:08:19,010
I'll try wiping the cup.

230
00:08:22,400 --> 00:08:22,800
Start.

231
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:33,700
Eight seconds.

232
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:40,880
I made an appointment
with Cui Xiangqin's doctor.

233
00:08:40,880 --> 00:08:42,010
Let's go over there.

234
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:46,160
She had

235
00:08:46,160 --> 00:08:47,560
rheumatic heart disease

236
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:50,200
and underwent valve replacement surgery.

237
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:50,800
Warfarin

238
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:51,720
and aspirin

239
00:08:52,120 --> 00:08:53,580
have contraindications.

240
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:57,000
How was her health condition
before she was murdered?

241
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:57,920
To be honest,

242
00:08:57,920 --> 00:08:58,780
it was very bad.

243
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:01,300
Did her condition worsen?

244
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:04,680
She had other postoperative complications,

245
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:06,520
and her condition had been unstable

246
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:08,160
for the past two months.

247
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:10,680
Who knew

248
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:11,660
about this?

249
00:09:12,080 --> 00:09:13,120
The patient herself

250
00:09:13,120 --> 00:09:14,180
and her secretary.

251
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:17,960
How did Cui Xiangqin react

252
00:09:18,200 --> 00:09:19,480
when she found out
her condition had worsened?

253
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:21,480
At first, she was very pessimistic.

254
00:09:21,840 --> 00:09:23,080
She talked to me many times,

255
00:09:23,080 --> 00:09:25,600
saying she wanted
to go abroad for treatment.

256
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:26,800
But for this disease,

257
00:09:26,880 --> 00:09:28,680
it's the same whether at home or abroad.

258
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:29,610
Later I found out

259
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:31,000
she was afraid

260
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:32,320
that if she didn't make it,

261
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:34,520
she could at least be with her daughter.

262
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:36,120
Why didn't she go abroad later?

263
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:37,520
She suddenly told me

264
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:39,320
she wanted to be treated domestically.

265
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:39,760
I guess

266
00:09:40,560 --> 00:09:42,890
she was too busy
with the company to leave.

267
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:44,600
When did this change happen

268
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:45,800
roughly?

269
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:48,400
Let me check.

270
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:52,960
I told her in mid-August.

271
00:09:53,880 --> 00:09:55,880
She came to me on September 4th.

272
00:09:56,640 --> 00:09:59,040
She was supposed to come
for a follow-up this week.

273
00:09:59,040 --> 00:09:59,760
I didn't expect her

274
00:09:59,760 --> 00:10:00,690
to just pass away

275
00:10:01,040 --> 00:10:01,920
so suddenly.

276
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:05,280
Come here, kids.

277
00:10:05,280 --> 00:10:05,940
Take a look.

278
00:10:08,560 --> 00:10:08,920
Here,

279
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:10,280
take a look too.

280
00:10:13,520 --> 00:10:14,040
My mom.

281
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:14,890
Let's go.

282
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:17,760
Chang Kaixin!

283
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:19,440
Chang Kaixin!

284
00:10:23,760 --> 00:10:24,520
What a coincidence.

285
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:25,450
Why are you here?

286
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:27,160
We still have some work to do,

287
00:10:27,160 --> 00:10:27,680
so we'll...

288
00:10:27,680 --> 00:10:28,320
Hello, Ma'am.

289
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:29,040
We'll get going now.

290
00:10:29,040 --> 00:10:29,840
Hello, hello.

291
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:32,680
